Z||000000||TooLowFiero||09-28-1999||02:02 AM||||i have bad cooling prob   my 84 se with the 2.5 l 4 popper hets up in like 30 seconds and also i was wondering what i can buy for it   i bought this 84 for 100 bucks so now i have an 86 2m4 and an 84 se coupe can someone help me||||reg||5
Z||000001||ChadMan||09-28-1999||08:55 AM||||If it heats up that fast, my #1 guess is bad thermostat (#2 is low coolant).<P>Park your car nose down, remove the thermostat cover, and remove the thermostat.  You should see coolant all the way up to the base of the thermostat housing.  If not, fill it up at the thermostat cover.  Once the coolant is at the proper level, replace the cover WITHOUT reinstalling the thermostat, then fire it up.  If it doesn't overheat, head down to NAPA and get yourself a new thermostat!<P>If it still overheats, time to completely flush and fill the system.  Visually inspect both the aluminum coolant tubes that run under the kick panels on each side of the car (don't laugh - I knew a guy got his 85 Coupe hung up on the edge of a loading dock and crushed a coolant pipe).  Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||TooLowFiero||09-30-1999||10:36 AM||||Thanks ChadMan i have bought a new thermostat since i work at an auto parts and service center (AllCar) today will be my work on fiero day i have the day off so now i have to do my new therostat shifter cable throttle cable (its really sticky) and bleed the brakes  thanks for you help =o)||||reg||10
